<article class="env-remark" id="0GPY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GPY">Remark <span data-tag="0GPY">91.2.8</span>.</a> Observe that in the situation of Lemma <a href="/tag/0GPX" data-tag="0GPX">91.2.7</a> we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^1_ A(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{A/A'}, N) = \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^1_ B(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{A/A'} \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} B, N) = \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^1_ B(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{A/A'} \otimes _ A B, N)  \]
</div>
  <p> The first equality by More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0GMT" data-tag="0GMT">15.61.3</a> and the second by More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FUY" data-tag="0FUY">15.87.1</a>. We have maps of complexes </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{A/A'} \otimes _ A B \to \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A'} \to \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}  \]
</div>
  <p> which is close to being a distinguished triangle, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00S2" data-tag="00S2">10.134.4</a>. If it were a distinguished triangle we would conclude that the image of $\xi $ in $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^2_ B(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}, N)$ would be the obstruction to the existence of a solution to (<a href="/tag/08S4" data-tag="08S4">91.2.0.1</a>). </p>
</article>